Description: Fix screencast format negotiation on PipeWire 1.6.x
 On PipeWire 1.6.x a variable-framerate screencast session (framerate == 0),
 as negotiated by per-window capture via ext-image-copy-capture, emitted an
 invalid maxFramerate choice and divided by zero in the param-changed handler.
 This made format negotiation fail with "no more output formats" (res -32),
 killing the stream. Skip maxFramerate when framerate == 0 in fixate_format
 and build_format, and guard the max_framerate division.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/emersion/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr/commit/896cee82a6f1
Applied-Upstream: 0.8.2
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-07-03
---
